Binary Search.
==================================================================================================================================================================
This Is the Big Idea

      We're not searching an array.
      
      We're searching the answer space.

==================================================================================================================================================================
Search space:

Minimum possible speed

↓

1

Maximum possible speed

↓

max(piles)

Every speed is a candidate answer.

==================================================================================================================================================================
Generic Pattern

          Whenever you see

                Minimum...
                
                or
                
                Maximum...

          ask yourself:
          
          Can I check whether a candidate answer is valid?

        If yes,
        
        there is a good chance Binary Search on Answer applies.
==================================================================================================================================================================
Example

Suppose

      Speed = 4

                Hours needed:
                
                ceil(3/4)=1
                
                ceil(6/4)=2
                
                ceil(7/4)=2
                
                ceil(11/4)=3
                
                Total = 8

Exactly valid.

    Can we do even better?

  Search the left half.

Suppose

          Speed = 2

          Hours:     2+3+4+6 = 15

          Too slow.

          Need a larger speed.

        Search the right half.
==================================================================================================================================================================
Binary Search Logic

                          low = minimum possible answer                          
                          high = maximum possible answer
                          
                          while(low <= high){                          
                              mid                          
                              if(mid works){                          
                                  answer = mid                          
                                  search left
                              }                          
                              else{                          
                                  search right
                              }                          
                          }


        Notice something.
        
        When mid works,  we don't stop.
        
        Why? Because we're looking for the minimum valid answer.




==================================================================================================================================================================
Generic Algorithm

                        Pick a candidate answer.                        
                        ↓                        
                        Can I verify it?                        
                        ↓                        
                        YES                        
                        ↓                        
                        Move Left                        
                        (looking for a smaller valid answer)                        
                        ↓                        
                        NO                        
                        ↓                        
                        Move Right                        
                        (need a larger answer)

