17. The Pattern You Should Remember

You now have several problems following almost exactly the same structure:

                    Koko Eating Bananas
                              Search: eating speed
                              Check: can finish within H hours?

                    Capacity to Ship Packages
                              Search: ship capacity
                              Check: can ship within D days?

                    Minimum Speed to Arrive on Time
                              Search: train speed
                              Check: can arrive within given hour?

                    Split Array Largest Sum
                              Search: maximum allowed subarray sum
                              Check: can split into <= K subarrays?

The general template is:

                    while (left < right) {
                    
                        long mid = left + (right - left) / 2;
                    
                        if (isPossible(mid)) {
                            right = mid;
                        } else {
                            left = mid + 1;
                        }
                    }
          return left;

The real skill is not memorizing the template. It's recognizing:

"If I guess an answer X, can I efficiently determine whether X is feasible—and does feasibility become monotonic as X increases?"

If the answer is yes, you should immediately think Binary Search on Answer.


